Rumo Use License

Copyright (c) 2026 Erik Pimenta. All rights reserved.

1. What is permitted
Anyone may, free of charge:
  a) access and use Rumo as published by the author
     (https://ravelroot.github.io/Circuit-Board-Bench-Lab/), for personal,
     educational or professional purposes;
  b) download Rumo (the repository or the files of a version published in
     Releases) and run it on their own computer, exactly as published, for
     the same purposes as above.

2. What is not permitted
Without the author's prior written permission, you may not:
  a) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the software
     or any part of it;
  b) sell, rent, license, sublicense, charge for access to, or include the
     software, in whole or in part, in a paid product or service;
  c) redistribute, publish, mirror or host the software at another
     address, even unmodified;
  d) reuse in other projects the code, the texts, the board and lab data,
     the drawings, the 3D models, the animations, the name "Rumo" or the
     logo;
  e) remove or alter the rights notices or this license.

3. Downloaded copies
Each downloaded copy is for the sole use of the person who downloaded it
and must keep this file. This license does not transfer ownership of the
software; all rights not expressly granted remain with the author.

4. GitHub platform
This license does not restrict the rights to view the repository and to
fork it within GitHub that the GitHub Terms of Service grant to its users.
No other rights are granted by such forks, including the rights to modify,
publish or sell.

5. Third-party components
The three.js library, the fonts and the third-party tools used by the
project remain under their own licenses, listed in the README.

6. Warranty and liability
The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. In no
event shall the author be liable for any damages arising from the use of,
or the inability to use, the software, including electrical builds made
from the labs.

7. Termination
Any use that does not comply with this license automatically terminates
the permissions in section 1, and downloaded copies must be deleted.

Permission requests: through the ravelroot profile on GitHub.
